ENTRY            M1070   20260817   20260928   20260928       M147
SUBENT        M1070001   20260817   20260928   20260928       M147
BIB                 15         57
TITLE      Photonuclear reactions on stable isotopes of cadmium
            and tellurium at bremsstrahlung end-point energies
            of 10-23 MeV.
AUTHOR     (F.A.Rasulova,A.A.Kuznetsov,V.O.Nesterenko,
           J.H.Khushvaktov,S.I.Alekseev,N.Yu.Fursova,
           A.S.Madumarov,I.Chuprakov,S.S.Belyshev,N.V.Aksenov)
REFERENCE  (J,CPH/C,50,064003,2026)
INSTITUTE  (4ZZZDUB,4UZ UZB,4RUSMOS,4KASKAZ)
            Faculty of Physics of Lomonosov Moscow State
            University.
FACILITY   (MICRT,4RUSMOS) MT-25 microtron.
INC-SOURCE (BRST)
METHOD     (ACTIV)
SAMPLE     Natural cadmium in metallic form and tellurium in
            powder form samples.
           The mass of target depends on bremsstrahlung end-point
            energy (Table 1):
                       EN-MAX, MeV            Mass, mg
                                       Cd            Te
                          10          475         1050
                          11          448         1100
                          12          454         1010
                          13          451         1060
                          14          451         1080
                          15          414         1000
                          16          417          220
                          17          427          190
                          18          401          100
                          19          389          110
                          20          113           90
                          21          116           90
                          22          116           90
                          23          112           90
DETECTOR   (HPGE) High purity germanium (HPGe) gamma-detector,
            ADC/MCA (CANBERRA).
MONITOR    (29-CU-65(G,N)29-CU-64,,SIG)
MONIT-REF  (M0920006,V.Varlamov+,J,BAS,80,317,2016)
CRITIQUE   M0920006 contains evaluated cross section of
            65Cu[(g,n)+(g,np)] reaction, not of 65Cu(g,n) one.
ANALYSIS   The gamma-ray spectra were processed using DEIMOS32
            code. The identification of the peaks was based on
            the gamma-ray energy and intensity and the half-life
            of the residual nuclei.
          The experimental yields of the reactions were
            normalized to one electron of the accelerated beam
            incident on the bremsstrahlung target and calculated
            using the formula (1) of the article.
           The cross-section per equivalent quantum for a natural
            mixture of isotopes included all possible channels of
            the final isotope production was determined by the
            expression (6) of the article.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The square root of the quadratic sum of all
            independent statistical and systematic uncertainties
            was used to determine the overall uncertainties in
            the results.
HISTORY    (20260817C) Data were compiled at the Russia MSU SINP
            CDFE by V.Varlamov.
ENDBIB              57
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           60
